ABSTRACT
================================================================================

The Hodge Complex Standard Model realizes the gauge algebra
su(3) + su(2) + u(1)^5 as a Lie subalgebra of the D4 commutant on the
14-mode multiplet, and identifies the physical hypercharge functional as
a specific element of the 15-dimensional sector-coarse space (HCSM-06,
HCSM-07). This paper establishes the orientation-flip Z2 symmetry of this
structure. We define the sector flip sigma on the 56-dimensional Hodge
sector V_56 = Omega^0 + Omega^1 + Omega^2 at lambda = 4 by the swap
(alpha_0, omega_1, alpha_2) -> (alpha_2, omega_1, alpha_0), induced by the
Hodge star identification Omega^0 = Omega^2. We prove: (i) sigma is an
involution (sigma^2 = I); (ii) sigma commutes with the D4 action; (iii)
under sigma, the sector operators transform as I -> I, F -> F, O -> -O;
(iv) the A_1 hypercharge coefficients transform as
(0, -1/6, -1/2) -> (0, -1/6, +1/2); (v) the B_1 coefficients transform as
(0, +1/2, +1/2) -> (0, +1/2, -1/2); (vi) the sector hypercharge values
transform by swapping Omega^0 and Omega^2; (vii) the multiset of
hypercharge magnitudes is invariant; (viii) the anomaly cancellation sums
are invariant; (ix) if the CKM and PMNS matrices depend only on the
multiset of hypercharge magnitudes, then their element magnitudes are
invariant under sigma while the Jarlskog invariant flips sign. The flip
exchanges the labels u_R^c <-> d_R^c on the A_1 block and
e_R^c <-> nu_R^c on the B_1 block, with no consequence for the magnitudes
of any framework observable. The framework therefore does not privilege
Omega^0 over Omega^2: the assignment of one color-triplet multiplet to
the outer sector and the other to the inner sector is a labeling
convention. All claims are HCSM-native and verified at machine precision.


