1.1 The orientation-flip question
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hodge Complex Standard Model (HCSM) derives the gauge algebra

    g_HCSM = su(3) + su(2) + u(1)^5                                   (1)

as a Lie subalgebra of the D4 commutant on the 14-mode multiplet
(HCSM-06 [HCSM-06]). The physical hypercharge functional is a specific
element of the 15-dimensional sector-coarse space of the 56-dimensional
Hodge sector (HCSM-07 [HCSM-07]):

    Y = sum_rho (alpha_rho I + beta_rho F + gamma_rho O) P_rho,      (2)

with A_1 coefficients (0, -1/6, -1/2) and B_1 coefficients
(0, +1/2, +1/2) uniquely determined by the Standard Model content and
the sector assignment (Input 3 of HCSM-07).

The present paper asks: does the framework privilege the sector Omega^0
over the sector Omega^2? These two sectors carry identical D4
decompositions 3A_1 + A_2 + 2B_1 + 2B_2 + 3E, and they are Hodge-dual to
each other. The assignment of u_R^c to one and d_R^c to the other was
fixed only by the ordering convention Y(u_R^c) < Y(d_R^c).

We prove that the framework admits a Z2 symmetry, the orientation flip,
that swaps Omega^0 <-> Omega^2 and fixes Omega^1, under which every
physical prediction of the framework is invariant up to a relabeling of
the color-triplet and lepton multiplets. The flip has no physical
consequence for the magnitudes of any observable.

