11. REPRODUCIBILITY
================================================================================

All numerical and algebraic claims in this paper are verified at
machine precision in IEEE-754 double precision, or exactly in rational
arithmetic. The verification script is provided in the HCSM companion
repository at 12-VERIFICATION/HCSM-09_verification.py. It constructs the
Hodge complex on Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8, the sector operators, and the
hypercharge functional, and verifies:

1. The sector flip sigma as an explicit Z2 action on V_56 (Lemma 4.1).
2. D4-equivariance [sigma, R] = [sigma, S] = 0 (Theorem 5.1).
3. The sector-operator transformation (25) (Theorem 6.1).
4. The coefficient transformations of Theorems 7.1 and 7.2.
5. The sector-value swap of Theorem 7.3.
6. The magnitude-multiset invariance (Corollary 8.1).
7. The anomaly preservation (Corollary 9.1).
8. The physical-prediction invariance of Corollary 8.3.

Running 12-VERIFICATION/run_all.py reproduces every numerical claim in
the HCSM paper stack.


================================================================================
12. CONCLUSION
================================================================================

This paper has established the orientation-flip Z2 symmetry of the HCSM
sector-coarse structure. The flip sigma, defined by the Hodge-star
identification of the outer sectors Omega^0 = Omega^2, is a well-defined
involution on the 56-dimensional Hodge sector that commutes with D4 and
swaps Omega^0 <-> Omega^2 while fixing Omega^1.

Under sigma, the sector operators transform as I -> I, F -> F, and
O -> -O. The hypercharge coefficients transform as
(0, -1/6, -1/2) -> (0, -1/6, +1/2) on the A_1 block and
(0, +1/2, +1/2) -> (0, +1/2, -1/2) on the B_1 block. The sector
hypercharge values swap Omega^0 <-> Omega^2, exchanging
u_R^c <-> d_R^c and e_R^c <-> nu_R^c.

All framework predictions of the magnitudes of physical observables are
invariant under sigma. The hypercharge magnitude multiset is preserved,
the anomaly cancellation conditions are preserved, and (conditional on
the flavor-sector dependence) the CKM and PMNS element magnitudes are
preserved while the Jarlskog invariant flips sign. The framework does
not privilege Omega^0 over Omega^2: the two outer sectors are Hodge-dual,
carry identical D4 decompositions, and are distinguished only by the
labeling convention for the orientation operator O.

The framework derives the space of hypercharge functionals (HCSM-06),
the coefficient values (HCSM-07), the anomaly cancellation (HCSM-08),
and the Z2 symmetry that acts on all of them (this paper). The Z2
symmetry closes the gauge-sector structure of the framework.


